{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_98","type":"agent_message","text":"The nuisance assertion is exposing a model gap, not just a weak test: feed currently contributes nitrogen but effectively no phosphorus, so algae pressure barely separates under control vs overfeed. I’m correcting that in the detritus dissolution path with a small dissolved-phosphate yield, which is a plausible v1 simplification and should make overfeeding causally affect nuisance the way the spec requires."}}
