{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_121","type":"agent_message","text":"# Implementation Notes\n\n## Decisions Made\n- Extended `TankSnapshot` with the chemistry, hardware, detritus, plant-health, and biofilter fields the five TUI screens need, so display stays snapshot-driven while actions still go only through `SimulationEngine`.\n- Added `tank_scenarios::ScenarioGeometryOverrides` and a startup selector so `cargo run -p tank_tui` can launch from the three preset scenarios with selectable size/fill presets before the main loop starts.\n- Implemented the TUI as a real binary with overview/chemistry/biology/actions/log screens, timed auto-advance, transient status messages for validation/load-save errors, JSON save/load, and action-form routing for all 12 `PlayerAction` variants.\n- Strengthened the regression suite by replacing the placeholder determinism test with a 720-hour scheduled run and by adding a dedicated 14-day overfeeding regression.\n- Added a small dissolved-phosphate yield in feed dissolution so overfeeding now has a causal path to higher algae nuisance, matching the acceptance behavior.\n\n## Spec Deviations\n- None.\n\n## Testing\n- Verified formatting with `cargo fmt --check`.\n- Verified the full workspace with `cargo test --workspace`.\n- Verified lints with `cargo clippy --workspace`.\n- Manual runtime entry point is `cargo run -p tank_tui`.\n\n---"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_47","type":"todo_list","items":[{"text":"Extend scenario materialization and snapshot data for TUI display needs","completed":false},{"text":"Implement tank_tui binary, screen renderers, input routing, save/load, and action forms","completed":false},{"text":"Strengthen determinism and overfeeding acceptance tests","completed":false},{"text":"Run fmt, tests, and clippy; fix resulting issues","completed":false}]}}
